#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68abb4f0-c532-5cb6-882c-dacfe6a945dc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using the General Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "1ab8245a-39fb-5633-b5ff-865ab17dbfb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4323" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-0.4,11 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,5,2 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b} & = {a}_{x} \\cdot  {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} \\cdot  {b}_{y} + {a}_{z} \\cdot  {b}_{z} \\\\  & = 0 \\cdot  2 + ( - 0.4 ) \\cdot  5 + 11 \\cdot  2 \\\\  & = 0 - 2 + 22 \\\\  & = 20\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bff08bf-0035-5f05-9607-493b301e8717" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given Two Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "dfc10727-c0d7-5b83-a4f6-afe3eb4831cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4324" :question/problem "Let \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}4 \\\\ - 2 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n and \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$." :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b} & = {a}_{x} \\cdot  {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} \\cdot  {b}_{y} + {a}_{z} \\cdot  {b}_{z} \\\\  & = 4 \\cdot  ( - 2 ) + ( - 2 ) \\cdot  5 + 1 \\cdot  t \\\\  & = - 8 - 10 + t \\\\  & = t - 18.\\end{array}$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0$, we obtain:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b} & = 0 \\\\ t - 18 & = 0 \\\\ t & = 18\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68abb4f0-c532-5cb6-882c-dacfe6a945dc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using the General Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b9c7bbd-a81a-5beb-99fb-69a24ae99e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056432} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e81485-e594-5a31-a714-8052d1c5515f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056433} {:answer/id #uuid "b26b218b-4861-55ea-a5f0-f6c5d20e9d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056434} {:answer/id #uuid "00e7b84f-f6bc-5c94-a534-276b5a94944a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056435} {:answer/id #uuid "5f3a85f9-f5e5-5513-867d-beff8976dd97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00e7b84f-f6bc-5c94-a534-276b5a94944a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056435} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4244e13-a09a-5a8f-a072-11e4298c8a78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056431}] :question/id #uuid "299fd51e-9aaf-5d57-966c-4d85ff141159" :question/math-academy-id "q-1340" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{u} = \\langle  - 3 , 2 \\rangle$ and $v = \\langle 7, 9\\rangle $. Find $u \\cdot v$."}]}
